ch a  no-brainer to include phone guy for  spooling out the series weird lore and  would also be a perfect fit for a cameo  appearance from the games developers and  original phone guy voice scott cawthon  hearing a tired coffin on the other end  of the line would be a nice nod to the  man who laid the foundation for a  phenomenon so remember these characters  hold a special place in the hearts and  children  okay foxy and friends it almost goes  without saying that a five nights at  Freddy's movie isn't going to work  unless Freddy brings the whole crew  inspired by the real-life arcade in  animatronics Pizza franchise  chuck-e-cheeses the five nights at  Freddy's series includes a whole  extended family of animatronic  entertainers and the movie would do well  to invite them all something jumping out  of the dark and grabbing you can get old  so the series animatronics all have  different attributes in the Chucky s  creepy child category there's Balloon  Boy and the wholesome yet homicidal baby  for eerie haunted circus ambience  there's the dancing Valora and the  clownish marionette the fleet-footed  foxy and the unsettling two theta are as  menacing as any slasher villain all of  these characters bring a different scary  skill set to the table especially if  they get the chance all of five nights  for to go into nightmare mode put a  quarter up one of the least talked about  aspects of the five night series is the  stuff that goes down between the levels  since the first entry the series has  featured little interludes of simple  Atari style minigames most of which seem  pretty normal on the surface the happy  vibe of the minigames stands in stark  contrast to the pitch-black horror of  the main game and also setup scares of  their own when the games take turns that  are unexpectedly grim haunted video  games have often been the stuff of  crappy creepypasta but they could serve  a purpose in the five nights movie  especially if the film is set in an  arcade tha